#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:423
msgid "Add the GARAN durability label to WooCommerce order confirmation emails"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:424
msgid "Shown to the customer only (never in the admin's copy), once per qualifying product in the order, on the processing, on-hold, and completed order emails, and on the customer invoice email."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:430
msgid "Short text line per product with a link that opens the label graphic"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:431
msgid "Full label graphic (embedded per product)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:432
msgid "Short text line per product, with the label graphic sent as a file attachment"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:434
msgid "\"Short text line\" keeps the email compact: product name and guarantee duration, with a link that opens that product's actual GARAN badge (brand/model/years) as a standalone image. \"Full label graphic\" renders that same badge as a real image directly in the email for every qualifying product — this adds real height with multiple products. \"Attachment\" keeps the same short text line but attaches each qualifying product's label graphic as a PNG file to the email instead of embedding or linking it. Rendered with the bundled font and template graphic (no server configuration needed); if that ever isn't possible it automatically falls back to the same short text line instead of showing nothing."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:439
msgid "Placed on a single product page with no attributes, it pulls the duration/brand/model straight from that product's saved EU Guarantee data (Product data → EU Guarantee) and only shows if that product actually qualifies."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:440
msgid "Or add the \"GARAN label\" block, which defaults to the same \"use saved product data\" behaviour, or fills in the same three fields with a live preview when turned off."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-eggl-settings.php:441
msgid "Give it years/brand/model explicitly — e.g. [eu_garan years=\"5\" brand=\"Acme\" model=\"AC-1200\"] — to override the saved product data and render unconditionally wherever placed, skipping the eligibility check. Uses the same display mode setting above either way. Also requires \"Enable\" above to be on."
msgstr ""

